{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2102","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2102","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2102\",\"parent_revision\":\"f5351a54b80736e6e8cd82176b0f19e1e468a3ad6c5df75e5f8bfa3d4da81213\",\"root_revision\":\"f5351a54b80736e6e8cd82176b0f19e1e468a3ad6c5df75e5f8bfa3d4da81213\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Status**: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING\\n\\nAll inputs are PRESENT and sourced from verified primary material.\\n\\n| Input | Status | Source |\\n|-------|--------|--------|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Item description: add proactive WebSearch pre-flight when prompt names a product/technology/version |\\n| Scope boundaries | AVAILABLE | Target state section: CLAUDE.md Critical Constraints or new `.claude/rules/fact-verification-first.md` |\\n| External interfaces | AVAILABLE | WebSearch tool, optionally `mcp__Ref__ref_search_documentation` |\\n| Existing system context | AVAILABLE | CLAUDE.md verified at `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/CLAUDE.md` lines 61\u201378; `fact-verification-first.md` confirmed absent; `fact-check` skill confirmed reactive-only |\\n| Verification expectations | AVAILABLE | Measurable signal section provides exact grep command and behavioral integration test |\\n| Constraints | AVAILABLE | Rule must be AI-facing behavioral constraint only \u2014 no implementation mechanics |\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add proactive websearch trigger when prompts mention specific named products/technologies/versions** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/ai-design-tools/huashu-design.md \u2014 pattern: Fact Verification First (Principle #0)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-03\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-04)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nThe gap is observable today by inspection:\\n\\n1. Open `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/CLAUDE.md` and read the Critical Constraints section (lines 61\u201378).\\n2. Note that the only verification trigger is hedging language: `\\\"likely\\\"`, `\\\"probably\\\"`, `\\\"I think\\\"`.\\n3. Run: `grep -l \\\"Fact Verification First\\\\|named product\\\\|Principle #0\\\" /home/user/claude_skills/.claude/CLAUDE.md /home/user/claude_skills/.claude/rules/*.md`\\n4. Observe: zero matches returned.\\n5. Prompt a Claude Code session: `\\\"Make a demo for DJI Pocket 4\\\"` \u2014 observe that the agent proceeds to plan/code without running WebSearch first.\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n- `grep` command above returns zero matches \u2014 confirms the rule does not exist.\\n- CLAUDE.md Critical Constraints section (lines 61\u201378) contains no named-entity trigger pattern.\\n- `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/rules/fact-verification-first.md` does not exist (confirmed by failed read).\\n- Source pattern: `research/ai-design-tools/huashu-design.md` lines 110\u2013112 \u2014 Principle #0 \\\"Fact Verification First\\\" from Huashu Design v2.0 (verified 2026-05-03).\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 Agent hallucination on named products/versions is a high-confidence, high-cost failure mode. The fix is a small rule addition with near-zero implementation effort. Without it, agents ship work grounded in nonexistent or outdated specs (e.g., a product not yet released, a library version that does not exist). The reactive `fact-check` skill does not mitigate this: it fires after content exists, not before planning begins.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Any task where the user names a specific product, technology version, or release event \u2014 the agent currently proceeds on training-corpus recall without WebSearch validation.\\n- Bottleneck: The absence of this rule is the structural cause of a class of hallucination bugs where the agent produces confident, detailed, but factually wrong output (wrong specs, nonexistent products, wrong API versions).\\n- Scope: All Claude Code sessions using this repository's CLAUDE.md as project instructions.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Eliminates a class of hallucination bugs at the root: proactive verification before any planning or code generation begins.\\n- WebSearch cost is ~10 seconds; cost of wrong assumption is 1\u20132 hours of rework (per Huashu Design Principle #0 rationale, `research/ai-design-tools/huashu-design.md` line 112).\\n- Complement to the existing reactive `fact-check` skill \u2014 this rule covers the pre-planning window that `fact-check` cannot reach.\\n- Consistent with the repository's existing verification discipline (hedging language trigger already in CLAUDE.md Critical Constraints).\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen a user prompt names a specific product (e.g., \\\"DJI Pocket 4\\\"), technology (e.g., \\\"React 20\\\"), library version (e.g., \\\"fastmcp v2.3\\\"), or release event (e.g., \\\"Gemini 3 Pro\\\"), the agent's first observable action is a `WebSearch` (or `mcp__Ref__ref_search_documentation`) call to confirm existence, current version, and release status. No planning, design, or code generation step occurs before this verification completes.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nOne of the following target states (either is acceptable \u2014 implementation choice is left to the planning phase):\\n\\n**Option A** \u2014 New rule file:\\n- `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/rules/fact-verification-first.md` exists.\\n- File contains a trigger table listing named-entity patterns (product name, version number like `v1.2.3`, release event terms) and the mandatory `WebSearch` action.\\n- CLAUDE.md Critical Constraints section references the new file.\\n\\n**Option B** \u2014 Inline in CLAUDE.md:\\n- CLAUDE.md Critical Constraints section contains a \\\"Fact Verification First\\\" block with a trigger table.\\n\\nIn both cases, the measurable signal grep returns at least one path. The rule must appear before planning/design/code-generation steps in the constraint ordering.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `grep -l \\\"Fact Verification First\\\\|named product\\\\|Principle #0\\\" /home/user/claude_skills/.claude/CLAUDE.md /home/user/claude_skills/.claude/rules/*.md` returns at least one path.\\n2. The matched file contains a trigger table or list of named-entity patterns and a mandatory `WebSearch` (or `mcp__Ref__ref_search_documentation`) action.\\n3. The rule is positioned before planning, design, or code-generation steps in the constraint hierarchy \u2014 not after.\\n4. A test prompt of the form `\\\"Make a demo for DJI Pocket 4\\\"` loaded into a Claude Code session causes the agent to run `WebSearch` as its first tool call before any other planning action.\\n5. The rule does not conflict with or duplicate the reactive `fact-check` skill \u2014 the two must address distinct lifecycle phases (pre-planning vs. post-content).\\n6. Linting passes: `uv run prek run --files .claude/CLAUDE.md` (and the new rules file if created) exits 0.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /fact-check \u2014 reactive verification skill; the proactive rule being added is upstream of this |\\n| Prior work | `/home/user/claude_skills/research/ai-design-tools/huashu-design.md` lines 110\u2013112 \u2014 Principle #0 source (verified 2026-05-03) |\\n| Prior work | `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/CLAUDE.md` lines 61\u201378 \u2014 Critical Constraints section where new rule should be anchored or referenced |\\n| Prior work | `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/skills/fact-check/SKILL.md` \u2014 reactive counterpart; must not be duplicated |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 standalone rule addition with no upstream blockers.\\n- Blocks: None directly; unblocks all future tasks involving named products/technologies/versions by ensuring pre-flight verification is in place.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\nNone \u2014 all inputs are AVAILABLE. Implementation can proceed immediately.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 the deliverable is a single markdown rule file (or an addition to an existing file) of ~20\u201340 lines. No code changes, no schema migrations, no tests beyond the grep check and one behavioral integration test.\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:8f2ddaee431a257fe9386a7928c9a2b4 -->\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/CLAUDE.md` triggers verification only on hedging language (\\\"likely\\\", \\\"probably\\\", \\\"I think\\\") \u2014 see \\\"Critical Constraints\\\" section. The reactive `/.claude/skills/fact-check/SKILL.md` runs after content exists, requiring an `UNVERIFIED` tag or backlog item to fire. Neither file declares a proactive pre-flight rule keyed on the prompt mentioning a specific named product, technology, version, or release. Grep of `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/` for `WebSearch first`, `named product`, `specific product.*search`, or `Principle #0` returns zero matches. As a result, an agent asked to \\\"build a demo using DJI Pocket 4\\\" or \\\"compare against Gemini 3 Pro\\\" can proceed using training-corpus recall without ever running a WebSearch, then ship work grounded in nonexistent or outdated specs.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAdd a proactive Fact Verification First rule to either `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/CLAUDE.md` Critical Constraints or a new `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/rules/fact-verification-first.md` and reference it from CLAUDE.md. The rule states: when a user prompt names a specific product, technology, library version, or release event, the first action MUST be a WebSearch (or `mcp__Ref__ref_search_documentation`) to confirm existence, current version, and release status \u2014 before any planning, design, or code-generation step. Add a one-row table of trigger phrases (named product, version number like \\\"v1.2.3\\\", release event terms) with the required verification action.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`grep -l \\\"Fact Verification First\\\\|named product\\\\|Principle #0\\\" /home/user/claude_skills/.claude/CLAUDE.md /home/user/claude_skills/.claude/rules/*.md` returns at least one path. The matched file contains a trigger table or list of named-entity patterns and a mandatory `WebSearch` action. A test prompt of the form \\\"Make a demo for DJI Pocket 4\\\" loaded into a Claude Code session causes the agent to run WebSearch before any other tool call.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"6496f194d6dd2805210352302a5f3d10eb6b8e4f8e7d6ff2b75f4d5a64d872a4\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCbm1Q\"}"}